{
  "id": "10111_omoikomi",
  "headword": "{思|おも}い{込|こ}み",
  "reading": "おもいこみ",
  "part_of_speech": "noun",
  "gloss": "assumption, conviction, preconception",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "assumption, conviction, preconception",
      "explanation": "A belief or idea that one holds firmly, often without sufficient evidence or that may be mistaken."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "10111_omoikomi_ex1",
      "japanese": "それはあなたの{思|おも}い{込|こ}みだ。",
      "english": "That's just your assumption.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10111_omoikomi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{思|おも}い{込|こ}みが{激|はげ}しい{人|ひと}だ。",
      "english": "They're a person with strong convictions.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10111_omoikomi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{自分|じぶん}の{思|おも}い{込|こ}みに{気|き}づいて、{考|かんが}えを{改|あらた}めた。",
      "english": "I noticed my preconceptions and changed my thinking.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "RELATED VERB:\n{思|おも}い{込|こ}む: to be convinced of, to assume firmly\n\nUSAGE NUANCE:\n{思|おも}い{込|こ}み can be:\n- Negative: when referring to unfounded assumptions or stubborn beliefs\n- Neutral/positive: when referring to strong conviction or dedication\n\nThe term often implies that the belief may not match reality.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {決|き}めつけ: jumping to conclusions (more negative)\n- {先入観|せんにゅうかん}: preconception, prejudice\n- {固定観念|こていかんねん}: fixed idea, stereotype",
